  "263": {
    "inputs": {
      "text": "How the reference pictures align with the target video — <Picture 1> (from [Shot 1]) aligns with the 0.00-second mark of the target video.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action, cinematic, extreme close-up of a lion's eye <Picture 1>. The golden iris is sharp and detailed, with the pupil slightly dilating as the lion begins to focus. The surrounding fur and long eyelashes are perfectly textured. The camera is static but the eye feels alive. Soft, warm savanna light.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:02.500, a new plan: The lion's face widens as it begins to snarl, showing its powerful teeth. Its whiskers twitch, and its powerful front paws start to shift and \"pitter-patter\" rapidly on the ground as it prepares to launch. Close-up shot.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:05.000, a new plan: The lion enters a full, powerful gallop across the savanna. The camera uses a low-angle tracking shot, moving parallel to the lion's body. Its mane flows backward with every stride, and its muscles ripple with intense power.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:07.500, a new plan: A new plan: A close-up shot of the gazelle's face, showing its large, expressive eyes wide with terror. Its ears are pinned back, and its nostrils flare as it sprints away from the predator.\n\n[Shot 5] At 00:10.000, a new plan: The lion reaches out with its powerful front paws, stretching its body in a massive leap to catch the gazelle. The camera captures the side-profile of the mid-air stretch, showing the intense connection between the hunter and the prey.\n\n[Shot 6] At 00:12.500, a new plan: The lion's paws narrowly miss the gazelle's side; the gazelle zips past. The lion performs a realistic \"stumble\" (kovyrk), its front paws landing slightly staggered as it absorbs the momentum. It finishes with a powerful tail flick and a slight head tilt.\n\noverall_soundscape: Deep, rhythmic breathing of the lion, the soft \"pitter-patter\" of paws on dry grass, the rapid thumping of the chase, and the final heavy landing.\n\nnon-diegetic_music: A cinematic, building orchestral score that starts with a low cello hum and swells into a majestic, sweeping string melody during the chase."
    },
    "class_type": "Text",
    "_meta": {
